leap71/PicoGKRuntime @ 0f26321c (26.2): IntersectImplicit passes millimetres
into an integer narrow-band parameter.

Proposal only. picovoxel, an unofficial community TypeScript/WebAssembly binding
of PicoGK (not affiliated with or endorsed by LEAP 71), ships the fix as
separate exports (Voxels_IntersectImplicitFast and its tape variant) so its
vendored runtime stays unmodified and the original stays available for
comparison. PicoGKRuntime PR #28 contains the identical hunk; the PicoPie
binding reached the same diagnosis independently.

`Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), fBackgroundMM())` sends the background distance in
millimetres into the constructor's `int nNarrowBand`. The implicit float-to-int
truncation gives (int)(3 x voxel size) instead of the configured band of 3
voxels: 3 at 1.0 mm by coincidence, 2 at 0.7 mm, 1 at 0.4-0.6 mm, and 0 below
about 1/3 mm, where the call throws. The intended value is the member the class
already holds, m_nSdfNarrowBand. One line.

Output values: unchanged where the truncation happens to equal the band (voxel
sizes from 1.0 up to 4/3 mm); at other sizes the temporary grid gets the
correct band, so the result's narrow band changes. Below about 1/3 mm the call
returns a result instead of throwing.

How picovoxel checks it (test/intersect-implicit.test.ts): at 1.0 mm the fixed
and original paths are value-identical; at 0.25 mm the original throws, while
the fix classifies identically to a reference construction built without the
truncation, with identical meshes.

Applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` to a pristine PicoGKRuntime 0f26321c tree.
Not applied by picovoxel's build; see upstream/README.md.

--- a/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
+++ b/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@
     {
         PKTRACE(Voxels_IntersectImplicit);
         
-        Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), fBackgroundMM());
+        Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), m_nSdfNarrowBand);
         
         CoordBBox oBBox = m_roGrid->evalActiveVoxelBoundingBox();
         
